This code defines a function `solve()` that takes no arguments. It reads the number of test cases from the input and for each test case, it reads the length of the binary string and the binary string itself. It then initializes a 2D array `dp` of size `(n + 1) x (n + 1)` where `dp[i][j]` represents the maximum cost of a substring of length `i` ending at index `j`. The maximum cost of a substring is the maximum of the cost of the substring without the last character (dp[i - 1][j - 1]) and the cost of the substring without the first character (dp[i - 1][j]) plus the cost of the current character. The result is printed for each test case.

